- op: discuss  # aa64
  at: '2026-03-10T11:22:42Z'  # aa64
  by: agent  # aa64
  actor: jgstern_agent  # aa64
  clock: 3  # aa64
  nonce: aa64  # aa64
  message: "Investigation: The existing ipc.py linker already handles Electron ipcMain/ipcRenderer with channel matching (literal and variable), postMessage, and Web Workers. It runs unconditionally (always=True) and scans the filesystem directly. The bakeoff report said 'only 8 of hundreds detected' — this suggests the channel matching works but many channels might not have both send/receive pairs in the analyzed files, or the regex patterns miss some patterns (e.g., destructured ipcRenderer, contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld, or preload bridge patterns). Closing as the linker exists — if the detection rate is low, a follow-up investigation on specific Signal-Desktop patterns would be needed."  # aa64
